[h1]TLB Keys[/h1]

Vehicle keys that your players manage in the field. Lock a vehicle for [b]your whole side[/b], for [b]your squad[/b], or to [b]one key[/b] in your pocket, all from the ACE interaction menu.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TLB-MilSim/TLB-Keys/main/docs/images/items.png[/img]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]CBA_A3[/b]
[*][b]ACE3[/b], built and tested against 3.21.2
[*]Arma 3 v2.14 or newer
[*][b]TLB Interactions[/b], optional. With it loaded, vehicle locks are picked on its hands-on lockpicking board, using its lock pick kit and paperclip
[*][b]TSP Breach[/b], optional. Its lock pick kit and paperclip pick vehicle locks as well
[/list]

[h2]Why[/h2]
ACE's vehicle keys open every vehicle of a side, and there is no good way to hand one out once a mission is running. A key is either in everyone's loadout or in nobody's.

TLB Keys replaces that with keys as real items. A vehicle nobody has locked is open, and the first player to lock one decides who else gets in.

[h2]The three ways to lock a vehicle[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Every key of the side[/b] - anyone carrying a blank key of the vehicle's side. The shared motor pool.
[*][b]The owner's squad[/b] - the owner's squad, carrying a blank key of the side. A squad's own truck.
[*][b]Paired keys only[/b] - only keys cut to that vehicle. The owner's key is cut as it locks. A command car nobody borrows.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TLB-MilSim/TLB-Keys/main/docs/images/lock-a-vehicle.jpg[/img]

Your unit chooses which of the three are allowed. Leave one on to enforce one way of working, or leave all three on and let the player who locks a vehicle decide.

[h2]What it adds[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Spare keys[/b]. Cut a blank key to a vehicle and hand it to someone. A spare always costs a blank key.
[*][b]Change locks[/b]. Every key cut for the vehicle stops fitting, spares included, when one goes missing.
[*][b]Master keys[/b], one per side. Opens and manages every vehicle of that side however it is locked, for Zeus, command and the motor pool. Can be hidden from the Arsenal.
[*][b]Key fobs[/b]. Program one to a vehicle and lock it from across the parking area, with a chirp.
[*][b]Key bindings[/b]. Lock or unlock the nearest vehicle your keys open without opening a menu, plus three key slots for chosen keys.
[*][b]Ignition lock[/b]. No key, no engine, even sitting in the driver's seat.
[*][b]Locked cargo[/b]. A locked vehicle's inventory stays shut to anyone whose keys do not fit.
[*][b]Inside handle[/b]. Anyone in a seat can lock and unlock, like a real car door.
[*][b]Hand over key[/b]. An ACE action on another player, so nobody swaps inventories.
[*][b]Inspect and label[/b]. See exactly which vehicles a key opens, and name it, so a crate of motor pool keys stays readable.
[*][b]Lockpicking[/b]. A lock pick kit opens a vehicle your keys do not fit.
[*][b]Hotwiring[/b]. Sitting in a vehicle you have no key for, hotwire it from the driver's seat. Picked and hotwired vehicles start without a key until someone locks them again.
[*][b]Vehicle types[/b]. Choose which kinds of vehicle use keys at all: cars, wheeled APCs, tanks, helicopters, planes, boats.
[/list]

[h2]Managing a vehicle[/h2]
The owner, and anyone with a master key, gets a Manage keys menu on the vehicle: who it opens for, cutting spare keys and programming fobs, changing the locks, naming it, handing it to someone else, or giving it up entirely.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TLB-MilSim/TLB-Keys/main/docs/images/manage-keys.jpg[/img]

[h2]Keys are items, and they stay items[/h2]
A key carries its cut in the item itself, so it survives being dropped, stored in a crate, handed to someone, saved in an Arsenal loadout and respawning. Take an enemy's key off a body and it opens their vehicles: keys belong to a side, not to a player.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TLB-MilSim/TLB-Keys/main/docs/images/keys-in-the-arsenal.jpg[/img]

[h2]Lockpicking and hotwiring[/h2]
A locked vehicle whose keys you do not have can be picked. Without TLB Interactions that is a progress bar, the way ACE does it. With [b]TLB Interactions[/b] loaded, the same action opens its lockpicking board and you pick the lock by hand.

[b]It works with the mods you already run.[/b] With TLB Interactions loaded, picking is its business: its board, its tools, its settings, including whether TSP Breach's kit is used. Without it, one setting picks between TSP Breach's kit and TLB Keys' own, and hides the other from the Arsenal, so players never see two kits for the same job. ACE's lockpick works throughout.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TLB-MilSim/TLB-Keys/main/docs/images/program-a-fob.jpg[/img]

Already inside a vehicle you have no key for? There is no lock left to pick, so [b]hotwire[/b] it from the driver's seat instead. Picked and hotwired vehicles start without a key until someone with a key locks them again.

[h2]Your keys[/h2]
Everything you carry is in one menu on yourself: inspect a key to see which vehicles it opens right now, label it, wipe it blank, put it in a key slot for a key binding, or use a programmed fob.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TLB-MilSim/TLB-Keys/main/docs/images/my-keys-menu.jpg[/img]

[h2]For mission makers[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Key Set module[/b]. Sync vehicles, crates and units: the vehicles are locked to the set, the crates hold its keys, the synced units spawn carrying one. Two modules with the same name share one set of keys.
[*][b]Master Key module[/b]. Synced units start with a master key for their side.
[*][b]Eden attributes[/b] on every vehicle: who it opens for, whose side it is, which key set it belongs to, whether it starts locked and whether its lock can be picked.
[*][b]Zeus modules[/b]. Lock or unlock a vehicle, strip its keys, drop a key for it, or hand a unit a master key.
[*][b]Scripting[/b]. Public functions to assign keys, hand them out and check who has access.
[/list]

[h2]Settings[/h2]
Around 40 settings under [b]TLB Keys[/b] in the CBA settings menu, all server-forced: which lock modes are allowed, who may lock a vehicle first, who may manage one, spare keys, master keys, key fobs, lockpicking, key bindings, the ignition and inventory locks, and which vehicle types use keys at all.

[h2]Dedicated servers[/h2]
The mod is signed. Copy [b]TLBKeys01.bikey[/b] into your server's [i]keys[/i] folder, and load the mod on the server and on every client.

